kind: llman.sdd.spec
name: "agent-session"
purpose: "Agent session management — session lifecycle, capability state, prompt construction, and turn orchestration."
valid_scope[3]: src/agent/session/,src/runtime_protocol/session.rs,src/domain/session_types.rs
requirements[34]{req_id,title,statement}:
  a1,"agent-session","System MUST provide AgentSession encapsulating prompt to model to tools to loop with full event stream, holding ONLY orchestration state; the system prompt MUST be assembled from injected context (AGENTS.md files, configured system prompt, append prompts) supplied by the composition root, NOT from a hardcoded fallback."
  a2,"turn-events","AgentSession MUST emit: turn_start, message_start, message_update (streaming), message_end events per turn."
  a3,"tool-events","AgentSession MUST emit: tool_execution_start, tool_execution_update (streaming partials), tool_execution_end events per tool call."
  a4,"model-switching","AgentSession MUST support cycleForward, cycleBackward, and select(model) for runtime model switching."
  a5,"thinking-level","AgentSession MUST support thinking level toggle (low/medium/high), clamped to model capabilities."
  a6,abort,AgentSession MUST support abort() to cancel current agent operation.
  a7,"context-usage",AgentSession MUST expose getContextUsage() returning estimated token count and context window percentage.
  a8,"session-persistence","AgentSession MUST auto-persist messages to SessionManager after each turn and after tool execution."
  a9,"prompt-construction","AgentSession MUST construct the full messages array: system prompt + context files + history + user prompt, prepended per turn."
  a10,"bdd-agent",BDD tests under tests/features/agent.feature MUST all pass.
  a21,"prompt-template","System MUST support forward-slash template colon name args syntax with positional arg substitution and all-args placeholder and default-value syntax."
  a22,"template-loader","System MUST load md files as prompt templates from global and project dot-xylitol-prompts directories and CLI-specified paths. Frontmatter provides description."
  a23,"slash-commands","AgentSession MUST expose get_commands returning builtin commands including model compact session fork stats export new resume plus extension-registered commands."
  a24,"command-dispatch","AgentSession prompt MUST intercept forward-slash prefix input dispatching to command handler or template expander before sending to LLM."
  a25,"resource-loader",System MUST provide ResourceLoader aggregating project context files from AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md plus skills and prompts and system prompt from CLI.
  a26,"bdd-agent-v3",BDD tests for prompt templates and slash commands MUST all pass.
  as27,"event-bus-lifecycle","AgentSession MUST integrate AgentEventBus to emit turn_start and turn_end events with auto-persistence of agent messages to session storage during the turn lifecycle."
  as28,"session-lifecycle","AgentSession MUST support start_new_session creating a fresh session with optional parent reference, and resume_session loading and validating an existing session including CWD assertion."
  as29,"bdd-agent-v4",BDD tests for AgentSession lifecycle and event bus integration MUST all pass.
  as30,"cohesion-decomposition",AgentSession MUST be decomposed into focused collaborator components covering model management and tool management and compaction orchestration and skill activation rather than a single object mixing many unrelated responsibilities.
  as31,"agent-renamed-from-session",AgentSession MUST be renamed Agent to reflect that it is the pluggable capability aggregate (models + io + tools + orchestration state) rather than a session persistence object; Agent MUST compose the decomposed collaborator components per as32 and MUST retain its existing event stream and public API surface so call sites only change the type name.
  as32,AgentSession 协作对象提取（落地 as30）,"AgentSession MUST be decomposed into named collaborator objects covering auto-retry (AutoRetryEngine), bash execution (BashExecHandler), and session export/import (SessionExporter). AgentSession MUST compose these collaborators as fields and MUST retain its existing public API and event stream (per as31). The session module MUST be reorganized into a session/ directory with focused submodules (io, retry, bash_exec, export, stats, prompt, steering) and AgentSession single-file size MUST drop below 600 lines."
  as33,"managers-extracted-to-siblings","AgentSession collaborators (ModelManager, CompactionOrchestrator, SkillManager) MUST live in dedicated modules under their owning subsystem (model/manager.rs, compaction/orchestrator.rs, prompt/skills.rs), not as orphan top-level files in agent/; AgentSession composes them as fields."
  as34,"sessionstore-port","System MUST define runtime_protocol::SessionStore abstracting session persistence; infra::session::SessionManager MUST implement it and a test in-memory double MUST exist under tests/support/; agent/ MUST hold the store as Arc<dyn SessionStore>."
  as35,"export-io-port","AgentSession's export_to_html, export_to_jsonl, and import_from_jsonl MUST perform file I/O through an injected Arc<dyn runtime_protocol::export::ExportIo> rather than calling std::fs directly, so that the agent layer remains free of filesystem side effects and future backends (gist, S3) can be added without changing agent code."
  as36,"bang-prefix-in-agent","The user-input bang-prefix parser (!cmd / !!cmd) MUST live under agent::session::bang, not in the domain layer, because it encodes CLI/agent interaction syntax rather than universal domain vocabulary."
  as37,"session-exporter-in-agent","Session export/import render and parse helpers (render_html, render_jsonl, parse_jsonl) MUST live under agent::session::export, not in the domain layer, because they are part of the export command orchestration."
  as38,"optional-bash-export","AgentSession MUST hold bash_executor and export_io as Option of Arc of the port trait; execute_bash and the export_to_html, export_to_jsonl, and import_from_jsonl methods MUST return a clear not-configured error when the corresponding slot is None, so a minimal conversation agent is not forced to carry bash or export capability."
  as39,"capability-state-on-session","AgentSession MUST own the runtime-mutable capability state (tools ToolSet, permission engine, hooks, active system prompt) so that Agent facade setters can mutate them and run can snapshot them per turn; AgentLoop MUST NOT duplicate this state, and the current duplication of hooks and tool_mode fields on AgentLoop MUST be removed."
  as40,"agent-rename-call-sites","The AgentSession to Agent rename MUST update every call site including agent/builder.rs, agent/runtime/react.rs, app/core/composition.rs, app/core/driver.rs, app/rpc.rs, app/server/rest.rs, tests/bdd.rs, and the public-API snapshot test; the snapshot MUST be regenerated and the rename MUST NOT change any behavior."
  as41,"permission-gate-extracted",A PermissionGate collaborator MUST hold the permission port and expose get_permission returning Arc<dyn XyPermission> so react.rs can keep doing tool_name to capability routing; the three dead check_permission_read/write/network wrapper methods (zero production call sites) MUST be removed.
  as42,"stats-compute-moved","The get_session_stats aggregation logic MUST move out of the Agent body into a compute function under agent/session/stats.rs taking the session store and session id; the Agent method MUST become a one-line delegate so the body holds no aggregation logic."
  as43,"trust-demoted-to-free-fn","The save_trust_decision method (which only reads self.cwd and does not hold a trust store) MUST be demoted to a free function under agent/session/trust.rs taking cwd, trust_store, and trusted; Agent MUST NOT carry this method since it has no cohesive reason to live on the capability aggregate."
  as44,"dead-code-cleared","After confirming zero production call sites via grep, the dead methods MUST be removed from Agent: the whole steering domain (steer, follow_up, clear_queue, pending_message_count, has_pending_steer, get_steering_messages, get_follow_up_messages, drain_queued_messages, message_queue, message_queue_mut), process_prompt, cycle_forward, cycle_backward, share_as_gist, registry_clone, set_append_prompt, compact_current_session, compaction_threshold, compaction_settings, register_template, register_templates, register_command, and register_skill_commands; dead #[allow(dead_code)] attributes MUST be removed alongside."
scenarios[42]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  a1,"prompt-from-loader",a project containing AGENTS.md and the CLI composition root constructs the agent,the agent builds its system prompt,the system prompt MUST include the AGENTS.md content and MUST NOT default to a hardcoded placeholder when the loader provides values
  a2,"turn-events","agent processes a tool-calling turn",turn starts,"events are emitted in order: turn_start message_start message_update* message_end turn_end"
  a3,"tool-stream",bash tool streams output,tool_execution_start fires,tool_execution_update fires multiple times then tool_execution_end
  a4,"switch-model",agent is running,cycleForward is called,next available model becomes active
  a5,"thinking-toggle",model supports thinking,thinking level is changed,new level is clamped to model capabilities
  a6,abort,agent is streaming a response,abort() is called,agent loop terminates and returns abort error
  a7,"context-usage",a model with 200k window is active,messages consume 50k tokens,getContextUsage() returns 25% and 50000 tokens
  a8,"auto-save",a turn completes,session is loaded from disk,the turn's messages are persisted
  a9,"prompt-build",system prompt is configured with context files,agent starts a turn,messages array has system prompt then history then user message
  a10,"bdd-pass",BDD runner invoked,"cargo test --test bdd",all agent scenarios pass
  a21,"template-expand",template has placeholder for first arg,template expanded with main.rs,content has main.rs substituted
  a21,"default-value",template has default for first arg,template expanded without args,content has default value
  a22,"load-global",prompts dir has review.md,templates are loaded,review template returned with description
  a23,"builtin-commands",get_commands called at startup,result is returned,result includes model compact session fork commands
  a23,"extension-commands",extension registers command analyze,get_commands called,result includes analyze command
  a24,"slash-dispatch","user sends forward-slash compact",prompt is intercepted,compact handler invoked
  a24,"template-dispatch","user sends forward-slash review with args",prompt is intercepted,template expanded and sent to LLM
  a25,"context-files-found",AGENTS.md exists in cwd tree,load_context_files called,returns AGENTS.md content as first entry
  a26,"bdd-pass",BDD runner invoked,cargo test runs,"all agent-v3 scenarios pass"
  as27,"turn-events-emitted",AgentSession has event bus subscriber,a turn starts and completes,turn_start and turn_end events are received by subscriber
  as27,"auto-persist",AgentSession has enabled session,agent message is received,message is persisted to session file
  as28,"resume-validates-cwd",a session file has cwd set to existing directory,resume_session is called,session loads successfully
  as29,"bdd-pass",BDD runner invoked,"cargo test --test bdd","all agent-v4 scenarios pass"
  as30,"responsibilities-separated",the session module responsibilities are enumerated,component boundaries are drawn,each component owns a single responsibility class
  as31,"agent-renamed-from-session","AgentSession was the 25-field capability aggregate called Session",the change is applied,"it is named Agent, composes the as32 collaborators, and retains its event stream and public API"
  as32,"retry-extracted","AgentSession holds retry_state and inline auto-retry logic exceeding 100 lines",the change is applied,"AutoRetryEngine collaborator exists, AgentSession composes it, and public retry behavior is unchanged"
  as32,"bash-extracted",AgentSession holds bash_cancel and inline !cmd / !!cmd handling,the change is applied,"BashExecHandler collaborator exists, AgentSession composes it, and bash-execution slash commands behave identically"
  as32,"export-extracted",AgentSession has inline export/import methods,the change is applied,"SessionExporter collaborator exists, AgentSession composes it, and export produces byte-identical output"
  as32,"api-retained",AgentSession public API (per as31),the session module is reorganized into a directory with submodules,all existing public method signatures and emitted events remain unchanged
  as33,"no-orphan-managers",src/agent/ is inspected,"the top-level files are listed","model_manager.rs, compaction_orchestrator.rs, and skill_manager.rs do not exist (they live under model/, compaction/, prompt/ respectively)"
  as34,"store-is-trait",the agent holds a session backend,the field type is inspected,it is Arc<dyn SessionStore> not Arc<SessionManager>
  as35,"export-io-injected",AgentSession is constructed for export,a write is performed,"the write goes through the injected ExportIo implementation, not direct fs calls in agent/"
  as36,"bang-in-agent",the bang parser is located,its module is inspected,it is defined under src/agent/session/bang.rs
  as37,"exporter-in-agent",export render helpers are located,their module is inspected,they are defined under src/agent/session/export.rs
  as38,"no-bash-configured",an agent is built without a bash executor,execute_bash is called,it returns an error mentioning bash executor not configured without panicking
  as39,"loop-no-dup-state",AgentLoop fields are inspected,the change is applied,hooks and tool_mode live on AgentSession only and AgentLoop holds only session and cancel
  as40,"agent-session-renamed",the source tree after the rename,"rg '\\bAgentSession\\b' src/ tests/ runs",zero matches remain and Agent is the capability aggregate
  as40,"snapshot-regenerated","the public-API snapshot existed for AgentSession",the snapshot test runs,it passes against the renamed Agent type after regeneration
  as41,"permission-gate-exists",the permission port was a bare field on the Agent,the change is applied,a PermissionGate struct holds it and get_permission still returns the Arc for react routing
  as42,"stats-delegate",get_session_stats held inline aggregation,the Agent method is inspected,"its body is a one-line delegate to stats::compute"
  as43,"trust-free-fn",save_trust_decision lived on the Agent,the change is applied,it is a free function in agent/session/trust.rs and the Agent no longer carries it
  as44,"dead-methods-gone",the steering domain and other dead methods existed,rg for those method names in src/agent/ runs,no production dead methods remain (only legitimately used methods survive)
